From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:26:34 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 45/60] Muse Spark: the drafter behind the lanes backend
 (opt-in), tf-muse dflash / drafted gates

engine.zig: the hello carries a drafts flag so followers build the same drafter. native.zig: TF_MUSE_DRAFTER names
the drafter pack on every rank; drafts stay off without it; a per-depth acceptance prior before a stream has its
own statistics. draft_main.zig: tf-muse dflash (the fixed protocol: greedy decoding drafting at every step, drafts
and optionally the taps dumped for the reference) and tf-muse drafted (plain greedy against the speculative loop,
PASS when every reply is byte-identical); one GPU, the one-GPU TP pair or two ranks.
